1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bygdebok for Ølen III page 379 Åsbø.
2 CONT
2 CONT To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/61316450/enger-asbe
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from Iowa Gravestone Photo Project. See photo on that website.
2 CONT See entry for her husband Andrew T Asbe for children & other information.
2 CONT
2 CONT *****
2 CONT MRS. ANDREW T. ASBE RITES HELD IN CHURCH NEAR KANAWHA THURS.
2 CONT FORMER KANAWHA RESIDENT DIES AT CLEAR LAKE 18 MONTHS AFTER MATE
2 CONT Kanawha—Funeral services for Mrs. Andrew T. Asbe, 83 , a pioneer resident of Norway township, who passed away at her home in Clear Lake Monday, Oct. 25 , were held Thursday afternoon at the Bethlehem Lutheran church with the Rev. 
2 CONC M. N. Peterson officiating. Burial was made in the Norway township cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingie Tollacksen was born in Fjelberg Parish, Norway, March 16, 1854, where she grew to womanhood. In 1875 she was married to Andrew L. Asbe and in 1881 the couple and their two children emigrated from Norway and settled on a farm
2 CONC  near Kanawha, where they lived until 1914, when Mr. and Mrs. Asbe retired from farming and moved to Clear Lake. Mr. Asbe died April 24, 1936.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Asbe is survived by three sons: Thomas of Belmond, Anfin of Kanawha, and Louis of Minooka, Ill.; and two daughters, Mrs. Henry Norwick, Morris, Ill., and Mrs. Ole Walker, Minooka, Ill.; 20 grandchildren and five great-grandch
2 CONC ildren. Besides her husband, three sons, Daniel, Tollef and Henry preceded her in death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Asbe took a prominent part in the work of St. John's Lutheran church near Kanawha and the Bethlehem Lutheran church of Clear Lake.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Asbe had been suffering from illness a week before her death, following failing health for over a year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Garner Leader and Garner Signal --- Garner, Iowa
2 CONT November 3, 1937
