1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ola (Ole) bought the farm Foss of his father in 1886. Six years later, he sold the farm and emigrated with the whole family to America. He got good advices from friends over there, we must believe. For example, Ola
2 CONC  Ormson Litlabø (Foss) and Johanna Ramsfjeld were both farmers in the area where he settled.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hilda's first and second men came from the same farm, Litlabø is a smaller part of the main farm Foss.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family used the surname Foss in America. We find some places Foss written as Faus, Ole as Ollie, Syvert as Servert, Anders as Andrew and Borghild written in many different ways - see "Navn, Name".
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/68055987/ole-o-foss
2 CONT
2 CONT Pictures from Foss farm (gard) to day:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.a-hotel.com/da/norge/133260-hjelmeland/6504783-1-fossane-gard/
