1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Aberdeen American News (SD) October 19, 1997 Section: MIDLAND OBIT Page: 3B
2 CONT
2 CONT DINA EIDET Dateline: WAUBAY- Article Text: The funeral for Dina Eidet, 86, of Waubay, will be at 2 p.m. Monday at Our Savior's Lutheran Church, Waubay. The Rev. Duane Neugebauer and the Rev. William Gregerson will officiate. Buria
2 CONC l will be in the Lakewood Cemetery, Waubay. Fiksdal Funeral Service of Webster is in charge of arrangements. Visitation will be from 1 to 5 p.m. Sunday, from 7 to 9 p.m. Sunday, and from 9 to 11 a.m. Monday, all at the funeral hom
2 CONC e in Webster. There will also be visitation on Monday prior to the service at the church in Waubay. She died Thursday, Oct. 16, 1997, at Lake Area Hospital in Webster. Dina Annette Hovland was born Sept. 16, 1911, to Thomas and So
2 CONC lvig (Tiegen) Hovland on the family farm in One Road Township, Roberts County, north of Ortley. She attended One Road No. 2 country school near her home and graduated from Sisseton High School in 1931. During and after high school
2 CONC , she worked doing housekeeping and cooking in the Stavig home in Sisseton. She married Paul Eidet on Oct. 28, 1939, at Sisseton. They lived and farmed southeast of Waubay. In 1955, they moved into Waubay, where they owned and ope
2 CONC rated Red Owl grocery store. In 1970, they sold the store to their son Dwayne. Her husband died in October 1971. She continued to work at the grocery store, living in an apartment above the store until her death. She was a member 
2 CONC of Our Savior's Lutheran Church of Waubay, was active in Circle and Women of the Evangelical Lutheran Church in America, and was a member of the Lebanon Lutheran Church Women. She was also a member of the Tuesday Club and the Waub
2 CONC ay Senior Citizens, where she had been serving as treasurer at the time of her death. She enjoyed candle making, egg decorating, cooking, baking and plate collecting. Survivors include one son, Dwayne (Dorothy) Eidet of Waubay; th
2 CONC ree daughters, Colleen Helwig of Upton, Wyo., Jean (Ken) Ness of Waubay, and Karen Eidet of Roseville, Minn.; three brothers, Anton Hovland of Seattle, Herman Hovland of Sisseton, and Clarence Hovland of Goodyear, Ariz.; three sis
2 CONC ters, Tilda Farness of Woodburn, Ore., Alice O'Brien of Yuma, Ariz., and Dr. Clara Riveland of Minneapolis; eight grandchildren; three stepgrandchildren; eight great-grandchildren; and five stepgreat-grandchildren. She was precede
2 CONC d in death by her parents, her husband, one son, one sister and one brother. Casketbearers will be Brian Helwig, Richard Breske, Gene Knapp, Jim Eidet, Michael Ness, Wade Eidet, Dennis Gall and John Anderson. Copyright 1997, 2007,
2 CONC  Aberdeen American News Record Number: 9710200084
