1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Funeral service for Herman Hovland was held on Saturday, October 15, 2005, at 2:00 p.m. at the Christian and Missionary Alliance Church in Sisseton, SD, with Rev. Steve Slaamot officiating. Organist was Steve Enebo
2 CONC e and music was provided by Curt and Linda Long, Lucille Crooks, Irene Hanson and Lloyd and Janet Bakke. Pallbearers were Scott Stangeland, Keith Stangeland, Brian Stangeland, Jeremy Ceroll, Eric Preston, and Kevin Tobeck. Honorar
2 CONC y Pallbearers were all of Herman's friends and family. Visitations were held on Friday, October 14, 2005, from 5:00 p.m. to 7:00 p.m. at the Cahill Funeral Chapel and also one hour prior to the service at the church. Interment was
2 CONC  at the Sisseton Cemetery. The Cahill Funeral Chapel of Sisseton, SD, was in charge of the arrangements.  Herman was born on July 7, 1913 to Thomas and Solveig (Teigen) Hovland in One Road Township, SD. He grew up and attended cou
2 CONC ntry school in One Road Township. After his education, Herman farmed with his father. While farming Herman starting working as a carpenter which he later became self-employed at and continued to work at throughout his life.  Herma
2 CONC n was united in marriage to Edith Erickson on November 10, 1938 in rural Sisseton, SD. Edith passed away on July 4, 1992.  Herman was the oldest member for the Gideon's in South Dakota and was a member for 57 years. He was also a 
2 CONC member of the Christian and Missionary Alliance Church in Sisseton.  Herman was a hard worker. He enjoyed reading the Bible and never missed reading every morning and every evening.  Herman passed away on October 11, 2005 at the T
2 CONC ekakwitha Living Center in Sisseton, SD. Herman is survived by two daughters, Beverly and Marlin Stangeland of Fridley, MN, and Bonnie and Jim Bucklin of Browns Valley, MN; son-in-law, Stan Sletto of Minneapolis, MN; two sisters, 
2 CONC Mrs. Alice O'Brien of San Diego, CA, and Dr. Clara Riveland of Virginia Beach, VA; one brother, Clarence Hovland of Sun City, AZ; nine grandchildren; and twelve great-grandchildren. Herman was preceded in death by his parents, Tho
2 CONC mas and Solveig; his wife, Edith; one daughter, Audrey Sletto; three sisters, Johanna Eidet, Dina Eidet, and Tilda Farness; and two brothers, Anton and Martin.
