1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ardyce Elmquist Posted: Tuesday, December 8, 2015 1:00 pm
2 CONT
2 CONT Ardyce Elmquist Ardyce M. Elmquist, age 85, of Watertown, passed away on Friday, Dec. 4, 2015, at the hospital in Watertown. She was the widow of Raymond Elmquist. Funeral services will be at 11 a.m. on Wednesday, Dec. 9 at the Br
2 CONC idge Church of the Christian & Missionary Alliance, 810 Jenson Ave. S.E. in Watertown. The Rev. Nate Yoder will officiate. Special music will be provided by Linda Long, Allen and Linda Hoekman and Ardyce’s nieces and nephews. The 
2 CONC family is requested to meet at the church on Wednesday by 10:30 a.m. for a prayer service. Visitation will be at the Crawford-Osthus Funeral Chapel in Watertown today (Tuesday) from 4 to 7 p.m. with a 7 p.m. prayer service. Visita
2 CONC tion will continue on Wednesday prior to services at the church. Burial will be at Mount Hope Cemetery in Watertown. Honorary pallbearers will be Irv Slaamot, Larry Crooks, Don Jensen, Robert Iverson and Friends of the Bridge Chur
2 CONC ch. Active pallbearers will be Calvin Hills, David Hovland, Paul Griepp, Dale Griepp, Dennis Elmquist and Dan Elmquist. Ardyce was born on Aug. 25, 1930, on a farm in One Road Township, rural Sisseton, to John and Inga (Hyllseth) 
2 CONC Hovland. She graduated from Sisseton High School and took a two-year teaching course. She taught grade school for six years. On Sept. 21, 1956, Ardyce married Raymond Elmquist, at Bethel Lutheran Church in rural Sisseton. She and 
2 CONC Ray lived at Thorp’s Cattle Ranch near Britton for nine months before moving to Watertown. Like Ray, she had a deep love for her spiritual family and her church, The Bridge, in Watertown. Ardyce had put her faith in Christ and sou
2 CONC ght to serve Him. As a couple, they were impeccably faithful about attending church services and functions. Ardyce dearly loved her natural family and her Norwegian heritage. She was very active in and enjoyed the Sons of Norway. 
2 CONC She was very sure to attend every extended family gathering and church function. Ardyce’s family was most proud of her when she spoke fluent Norwegian with other vacationers while on trips to the Canadian Rockies or when in Norway
2 CONC . Ardyce is survived by her two sons, Daniel (Sandy) Elmquist and Dennis Elmquist, all of Watertown. She was preceded in death by her husband, Raymond; one daughter, Cheryl; her parents; two brothers; and five sisters. For more in
2 CONC formation go to www.crawfordfuneralchapel.com.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.thepublicopinion.com/obituaries/ardyce-elmquist/article_e65c79d2-9dc3-11e5-b5dc-1f96a3906c3e.html
