1 NAME Fredrikke Wilhelmine /Ebbell/
2 GIVN Fredrikke Wilhelmine
2 _MARNM Ebbell
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 4 SEP 1810
2 ADDR
3 STAE Østfold
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 MAR 1851
2 PLAC Ørmen
2 ADDR
3 STAE Østfold
3 CTRY Norge
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The text below was translated from an article in the history journal Varden “En fremmed fugl kommer til Ørmen (Frederikke Wilhelmine Ebbell), 1991, Isaksen, Per Chr.” which was published by the Onsøy Historical Soc
2 CONC iety in Fredrikstad municipality.
2 CONT Note: The translation used a free on-line translator and errors in translation may be present. Only the first part of the article has been included below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT “A Strange Bird Comes To Ormen 
2 CONT
2 CONT One day in 1815, a 5-year-old girl named Frederikke Wilhelmine comes with her parents to Mellem Ormen vestre. The father is Examinatus Juris Lars Smith Ebbell and the mother his housekeeper Helene Nilsdtr. For some reason, the par
2 CONC ents are not married, but the daughter is <<desired in gender and character>> and thus fully entitled to inherit as a child born within marriage. Frederikke Wilhelmine, commonly called Mina, was confirmed at Onsoy Church on Octobe
2 CONC r 1, 1826, by the pastor because she lived with her father. The father, merchant Lars Smith Ebbell, had already in May 1824, appointed his daughter as sole heir. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Already at 20 years old, on July 5, 1830, she got engaged to her peer neighbor Hans Tonnesen from Mollestad, son of Tonne Sebiornsen and Gunild Larsdtr. They had a total of 9 children, of whom 6 grew up and got married. Four boys 
2 CONC and two girls. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The eldest of the boys, Theodor, grew up on the family farm and acted as the father did when he passed away in 1850. He became a very well-known and respected man in the village. Besides being a skilled farmer, he held many positi
2 CONC ons of trust. Here it is only mentioned that he was postmaster in Onsøy at one point, acting sheriff after sheriff Gundersen's passing, a member of Onsøy Savings Bank's board for 34 years, and bank director for 10 years until he r
2 CONC etired at the age of 80. He was also the mortgage bank's appraiser for Onsøy, and so on. Theodor married Mathea Nilsdtr, daughter of Nils Olsen from Ormen Østre. They had 10 children. Theodor Hansen passed away on New Year's Day 1
2 CONC 923 at the age of 92. The second of the boys, Andreas, trained as a tailor and worked as a farmer and tailor for some time until he moved with his family in 1874 to Glemmen. The third of the boys, Carl, got married at Strømnes in 
2 CONC Råde and settled there as a farmer. The youngest of the boys, Gundro, moved already in 1873 to the suburb. The eldest of the girls, Nicoline, got married in 1862 to Melchior Glamer from Switzerland, who was employed at Kjølberg. T
2 CONC hey moved immediately after the wedding to Borregaard in Tune, because he was a cattle breeder. According to Tune in 1865, they lived at Borregaard with daughter Margrethe, 4 years old. According to the Tune church book, he emigra
2 CONC ted on 7.12.1875 to Sarpsborg. The youngest of the children, Helmine Lovise Frederikke, got married in 1873 to the widower Jens Christian Johnsen, who grew up in Ørmen and was trained as a teacher at Asker Seminary. He worked as a
2 CONC  teacher for a few years but later joined the police force, residing in Fredrikshald. He was a well-known personality in the town, mentioned in the book <<800 Halden Profiles>>.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Christian lived in Fredrikshald in 1908, the widow Helmine Lovise Frederikke moved to Oslo, where she died in 1937. They had a total of 10 children, all of whom grew up, got married, and had descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of Helmine Lovise Frederikke's great-grandchildren was recently in contact with Onsoy Historical Society regarding the family in Ørmen. She was so kind to provide us with the names and other data on these 10 children and the f
2 CONC urther growth of the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Who was Frederikke Wilhelmine Ebbell, who came to Ormen at about 5 years old, settled there, and had a total of 9 children and several grandchildren? Where did she come from, and where were her ancestors from? Unfortunately, we ha
2 CONC ve not yet been able to find out where her mother’s family comes from…………..”
